{"conversation_id":"9e1a4d71-de54-4e88-a2fd-09c74e012bd9","status":"SUCCESS","response":"### Findings\n\n| Severity | File:Line | Invariant | Recommended Correction |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| — | [lower.cljc:731-768](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-py-fstrings/src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc#L731-L768) | **Evaluation Order \u0026 Evaluate-Once (Mandatory Check)**: Interpolated expressions must evaluate strictly once, in source order (left-to-right) at runtime when string concatenation executes, with no eager lowering-time or lazy runtime hazards. | None. Invariant holds: [lower-strings](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-py-fstrings/src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc#L731-L768) lowers expression parts into a single runtime sequence under `(app* 'py/str (apply app* 'data/str-concat ...))`, where operands evaluate left-to-right. Confirmed by e2e pin [e2e_test.clj:936-944](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-py-fstrings/test/yang/python/antlr/e2e_test.clj#L936-L944) (`tick(1)` and `tick(2)` side effects print `1`, `2`, `3 5`). Format specifiers remain raw string literals at lowering and are parsed/validated at runtime via `py/format-spec`. |\n| — | [lower.cljc:470-768](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-py-fstrings/src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc#L470-L768), [prelude.cljc:3033-3380](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-py-fstrings/src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc#L3033-L3380), [lower_test.clj:638-735](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-py-fstrings/test/yang/python/antlr/lower_test.clj#L638-L735), [e2e_test.clj:920-1010](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-py-fstrings/test/yang/python/antlr/e2e_test.clj#L920-L1010) | **Resume Seam (Mandatory Check)**: The resume-by-state handoff across the interruption boundary (zcode-subagent to glm-5.3) must introduce no style discontinuities, duplicate definitions, dangling symbols, or half-finished branches across touched files. | None. Invariant holds: the four files exhibit